  "question": {
    "text": "Given sum of the first $n$ terms of an A.P. is $2 n+$ $3 n^2$. Another A.P. is formed with the same first term and double of the common difference, the sum of $n$ terms of the new A.P. is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FPqOc",
      "text": "\n$n+4 n^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GBvMT",
      "text": "\n$6 n^2-n$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "QbVg6",
      "text": "\n$n^2+4 n$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ftYWq",
      "text": "\n$3 n+2 n^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\mathrm{S}_n=2 n+3 n^2$\nNow, first term $=2+3=5$\nsecond term $=2(2)+3(4)=16$\nthird term $=2(3)+3(9)=33$\nNow, sum given in option (b) only has the same first term and difference between 2 nd and 1 st term is double also.",
